# Text files are checked out with LF line endings on every platform, whatever
# core.autocrlf says. The tests read sources, fixtures and goldens byte for
# byte: with CRLF, the grammar corpus finds no code block under its headings,
# and generated files no longer match what they are generated from. Binary
# files (PNG, TTF, VSIX) are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF line endings: with LF only, cmd.exe can
# fail to find a GOTO or CALL label, and tools/release.cmd uses several.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
